{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Cakkhupāla","html":"<article id='thag1.95'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.95 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.95 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dasamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Ten </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Cakkhupālattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Cakkhupāla </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Andhohaṁ hatanettosmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’m blind, my eyes are ruined, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kantāraddhānapakkhando; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’m traveling a desolate road. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sayamānopi gacchissaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Even if I have to crawl I’ll keep going—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na sahāyena pāpenā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>though not with wicked companions. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Cakkhupālo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
